# arduino-cli's intermediate build tree — ~38 MB of objects, cores and archives, regenerated by
# any `arduino-cli compile`. Nothing here is needed to flash a board.
#
# The flashable image *is* tracked, deliberately: `build/wlc_sniffer.ino.bin` and its three
# siblings are the restore/rollback source the README tells people to flash from, and the
# offsets in `flash_args` are the record of where each goes. Keep those in step with the sketch —
# a stale restore image silently downgrades a board, which is worse than not having one.
build/esp32.esp32.esp32c5/

# Link-time artifacts, ~38 MB, regenerated by any compile. These live beside the tracked
# restore image rather than under the intermediates directory above, so the rule there does
# not cover them — `git add firmware/wlc_sniffer/` swept all three into a commit on
# 2026-09-03 before this was added.
#
# Only the four files the README flashes from are tracked: wlc_sniffer.ino.bin, its
# .bootloader.bin and .partitions.bin, and boot_app0.bin — plus flash_args, which records
# the offsets. Nothing here is needed to flash a board.
build/wlc_sniffer.ino.elf
build/wlc_sniffer.ino.map
build/wlc_sniffer.ino.merged.bin
